{"id":219,"flavor":[{"games":["Alpha Sapphire"],"text":"Magcargo’s body temperature is approximately 18,000 degrees Fahrenheit. Water is vaporized on contact. If this Pokémon is caught in the rain, the raindrops instantly turn into steam, cloaking the area in a thick fog."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Magcargo’s shell is actually its skin that hardened as a result of cooling. Its shell is very brittle and fragile—just touching it causes it to crumble apart. This Pokémon returns to its original size by dipping itself in magma."},{"games":["Y","Crystal"],"text":"Its body is as hot as lava and is always billowing. Flames will occasionally burst from its shell."},{"games":["X","SoulSilver","FireRed","Silver"],"text":"Its brittle shell occasionally spouts intense flames that circulate throughout its body."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Its body temperature is roughly 18,000 degrees F. Flames spout from gaps in its hardened shell."},{"games":["HeartGold","LeafGreen","Gold"],"text":"The shell on its back is just skin that has cooled and hardened. It breaks easily with a slight touch."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"The shell on its back is made of hardened magma. Tens of thousands of years spent living in volcanic craters have turned MAGCARGO’s bodies into magma."},{"games":["Sapphire"],"text":"MAGCARGO’s body temperature is approximately 18,000 degrees F. Water is vaporized on contact. If this POKéMON is caught in the rain, the raindrops instantly turn into steam, cloaking the area in a thick fog."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Magma Armor","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon’s hot magma coating prevents it from being frozen."},{"name":"Flame Body","hidden":false,"description":"Contact with the Pokémon may burn the attacker."},{"name":"Weak Armor","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon's Defense stat is lowered when it takes damage from physical moves, but its Speed stat is sharply boosted."}],"eggGroups":